  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "rei-snacktime-draw-vs-exhausting",
      "title": {
        "en": "Rei Snacktime, Draw vs Exhausting"
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "card-list",
          "items": [
            {
              "cardId": "c_1056_srt4",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            },
            {
              "cardId": "c_1056_uni1",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Rei Additive/Multiplicative Damage Bonuses"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Rei is one of the best pure Damage Buffers in the game\nVoid, Basics, Multi Hit and 1 cost or lower are her buff Synergies\nRei usually increases damage through Additive Damage Increases\nAdditive Damage Increases have amazing synergy with Multi Hit/Attack Spam\nExamples:\nChizuru Oni 1 Base\n50% x 4 = 200%\nBut with a 40% Additve Damage Increases from Rei\n(50%+40%) x 4 = 360%, from only 40% Additive, a 1.8x Damage Increase!\nWhile 40% Multplicative Damage would only be\n(50%x140%) x4 = 280% from 40% Multiplicative, only 1.4x Damage Increase\nRei is Capable of a huge ammount of Additive Damage Increase\n60/40% from Resonating Darkness\n150-50% from Resonating Darkness\n80% from 4 Moral\n290% for a Multi hit Attack or 140% Permanently Possible before Dupes"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "card-list",
          "items": [
            {
              "cardId": "c_1056_uni2",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            },
            {
              "cardId": "c_1056_uni2",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Rei's other strength is her ability to Deck Thin\nRei's Snacktime is capable of Exhausting Cards\nExhaust means the card will be gone for the rest of the Combat\nSnacktime means you can keep bad cards like Basics, but just get rid of them\nExhausting 2 cards with Snacktime is strong\nExample:\nYour 24 card deck after Exhausting 3 (2+Itself) means you have a 21 card deck\nThe only possible problem with Snacktime, is it isn't a card positive usually\nExample:\n5 Cards in hand\n2 Cards in hand, Snacktime Exhausts 3 (2+Itself) 5-3\n4 Cards in hand, Snacktime draws 2 2 + 2\n-1 Card in hand compared to before Snacktime\nYou need supplemental Card positive draw most times"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Upgrade and Retain can also mean Exhaust"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "card-list",
          "items": [
            {
              "cardId": "c_1056_srt4",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            },
            {
              "cardId": "c_1056_srt4",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            },
            {
              "cardId": "c_1056_srt4",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Exhaust means the card can't be Used/Drawn again for the rest of combat\nUpgrades are used up and become permanent efffects, effectively Exhaust\nRetain cards stay in Hand until used/discarded, effectively Exhaust\nRei as a character has a very thin deck once you use everything\nUp to 4 Thinner deck (Strike, Resonating, Condensation) and Snacktime"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
